# Listening material cut for his ear and delivered as attachments: boundary
# clips, their zips, the self-contained player pages that carry the audio inline,
# and the line-run chart. None of it is a KUT — a KUT lives permanently in the
# KFI, NMW, and these are evidence he can discard once he has ruled. Keeping
# hundreds of MB of his own masters in a source repository would also be the
# opposite of that law.
BLK-TEST-CLIPS/
BLK-TEST-ZIPS/
LISTEN/
LINE-RUNS-ANALYSIS.svg

# Delivered to him directly; the audio never belongs in a source repo.
IRREPLACEABLE/
IRREPLACEABLE-PARTS/

# Marking pages for the staged works — a whole song embedded in each so he can
# set boundaries by ear. Delivered to him directly. Rebuilt from the KFI whenever
# it is wanted, so nothing is lost by keeping 392 MB of his own audio out of a
# source repo.
MARK/

# VTPP — the one listening tool, a whole song embedded per work so he taps the
# frame his voice arrives and leaves rather than types a time. Delivered to him
# directly and rebuilt from the KFI on demand by scripts/kkr/build-vtpp-v1.mjs.
VTP/

# A/B renders cut so his ear can settle a question arithmetic cannot — which of
# two endings is the ending. Same class as the rest here: evidence he discards
# once he has ruled, reproducible from the master, and never a KUT.
TRIAGE/
